\begin{defn}\label{def:vc}\emph{\cite[Definition 2]{rock-vietnam}}
A lsc function $f:\Rn\rightarrow\overline{\R}$ is called variationally convex at $\bar x$ for $\bar v\in\partial f(\bar x)$,
if for some convex neighborhood $U\times V$ of $(\bar x, \bar v)$ there exist a lsc convex function $\varphi\leq f$ on $U$ and a number $\varepsilon>0$ such that
$[U_{\varepsilon}\times V]\cap \gph\partial f=[U\times V]\cap \gph \partial \varphi\text { and } f(x)=\varphi(x) \text{ at the common element $(x,v)$,} $
where $U_{\varepsilon}:=\{x\in U|\ f(x)< f(\bar x)+\varepsilon\}$.
\end{defn}

